breaking news here in germany where  authorities have arrested two former  soldiers on terror charges federal  prosecutors accused the men of  attempting to form a mercenary group to  fight in yemen prosecutors say the plot  involved former soldiers and police  officers the veterans were taken into  custody following raids on their  apartments in southern germany on  wednesday morning  dw political correspondent jared reed is  following this story welcome jared what  more do we know about these people and  their motives  well phil as you say these two former  soldiers were arrested on wednesday  morning and according to investigators  they wanted to form a sort of private  army made up of up to 150  personnel with the view to fight in the  civil war in yemen and according to uh  investigators these two former soldiers  were aware that this would involve acts  of killing including of  civilians and what they say is that the  primary motivation for this was money  the view to be paid up to 40 000 euros  per soldier  per month and what they had set out to  do was to try and get third parties to  finance this particularly saudi arabia  which as we know has led the military  intervention in  yemen according to investigators at  least one of these soldiers repeatedly  tried to make contact with saudi arabia  make connections with saudi officials  but  to no avail apparently saudi arabia  never responded to to these approaches  what we also do know too is that they  have been hit with terrorism-related  charges and they're going to appear  before an investigating judge at the  german federal court of justice later on  wednesday  now this isn't the first scandal to hit  germany's armed forces does the  bundeswehr have a problem  well sections of the bundeswehr do have  a problem with extremism particularly  the elite military wing of the german  armed forces this is a branch called the  ksk and over the years germany's  military counter intelligence  office has investigated several dozen  ksk members for suspected extreme  right wing tendencies uh one section of  the ksk was actually disbanded by the  german defense minister last year she  also threatened that the whole operation  could be disbanded if it didn't uh clean  up its act  what we know more broadly in the  bundeswehr from a report last year is  that currently some 500 soldiers in the  german military are being investigated  for uh right-wing extremism all right  thank you for that dw political  correspondent jared reed
 

